  <string name="menus_service_label">Berpiztu AI Keyboard: menus and colours</string>
  <string name="menus_service_summary">Moves the keyboard out of the way of the menus that open, and sees an app\'s colour for Theme › Per app</string>
  <string name="menus_service_description">Berpiztu AI Keyboard sees only the field it types in. With this on, it also sees where a menu opens, an app\'s or a list that drops down, to move out of its way (Preferences › Also move out of the way of menus); and, with Theme › Colours › Per app, the colour just inside the field it types in, to take the app\'s colour (App\'s). It reads nothing else.</string>
  <string name="menus_watch_off">Let it see the menus</string>
  <string name="menus_watch_off_summary">Android shows other apps\' menus only to an accessibility service: a tap turns on Berpiztu AI Keyboard: menus</string>
  <string name="voice_lan">Local network (IP)</string>
  <string name="voice_remote">Remote</string>
  <string name="voice_lan_hint">The IP of the computer with ia-voice on your network, such as 192.168.1.20; port 8060 unless you write another.</string>
  <string name="headset_box">The headset\'s own keyboard</string>
  <string name="headset_box_summary">On the glasses, the keys filling the box the headset gives a keyboard; off, the phone\'s keyboard, as any Android keyboard. It changes when the keyboard opens again</string>
  <string name="menus_watch_grant">First let the app turn things on by itself: pair it in Wireless debugging, then tap Let it see the menus again</string>
  <string name="windows_licences_summary">FUTO swipe-library (GPL-3.0), FUTO Swipe models (FUTO Model Weights License 1.0), ExecuTorch (BSD), AOSP LatinIME word lists, Vortice.Windows (MIT), NAudio (MIT), Material Symbols (Apache-2.0)</string>
  <string name="avoid_menus_electron">VS Code and other Electron apps tell their menus only when started with --force-renderer-accessibility: add it to their shortcut (Properties › Target, after Code.exe).</string>
